CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ both destructors ran exactly once: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ destroyed in reverse order: B before A: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ object declared before the try not yet destroyed: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
[except.ctor]/1-3, [except.throw]/4: automatic objects constructed in the try
are destroyed in reverse order during unwinding, before the handler; an object
declared before the try is not destroyed by the handler.  Non-vacuous.
